    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 970,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 280,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "label": "Build Environment Context",
        "nodeType": "environment_context_builder",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "ENVIRONMENT ACTION SELECTOR\nUse the instruction, activePersona, sensory evidence, taskState, decisionRequirements, and capabilities. Persona shapes tone without inventing facts. History and memories are context, never current sensory proof.\n\nReturn strict JSON with exactly response, actions, movementRequest, and taskDecision. Select at most one action. response is the robot's actual reaction or utterance, not a plan or workflow explanation. taskDecision includes outcome, reason, objectiveComplete, continuationPolicy, requiredCompletionBasis, and presentation. Set presentation to conversation only when response should be spoken; otherwise use private. Physical work also needs motionClass and actionPurpose: expression, information_gain, or task_effect. information_gain requires bounded visual_observation. Expression normally requires action_result unless taskState requires later evidence.\n\nWhen mustSelectAction is true, return one safe advertised action now. Prefer one exact advertised robotCommand whenever it satisfies the instruction. Use movementRequest only for genuinely off-script body_local motion when robotMotionPlan is advertised. Never combine movements. If action is selected, response may refer only to that action and must not imply it already happened. If action is impossible, report why without future-action prose.\n\nTaskState evidence proves the whole objective after an action; it never replaces the required current action. An action has not happened: use outcome act and objectiveComplete false. Preserve taskState and complete only from its required evidence. Use only current capabilities and capabilityRules. The camera sees the external scene, not the robot.\n\nFor autonomy, stillness may be appropriate, but cognitive silence or generic nothing-actionable text is not. Produce a persona-grounded private reflection, deliberate conversation, or bounded action. With a fresh image, provide a concise observationSummary.",
          "recentHistoryLimit": 4
        }
      }
    },
